      "title": "A supercritical nonuniqueness example on a graph roughly isometric to the square lattice",
      "SEO_title": "A supercritical nonuniqueness example on a graph roughly isometric to the square lattice | Alec Kriebel",
      "description": "An explicit graph roughly isometric to the square lattice has positive-probability nonuniqueness at p=19/20 above its critical threshold, for a declared reading of Problem 9.6.",
      "rights": "CC BY 4.0; authored code separately MIT",
      "abstract": "We give an explicit deterministic graph of maximum degree four, roughly isometric to the square lattice, on which iid bond percolation has at least two infinite clusters with probability greater than one third at parameter 19/20, while its critical probability is at most 9/10. Edges internal to two opposite quadrants are retained; every other lattice edge is replaced by a path of length 100. Elementary dual parity and all-distance path bounds prove the assertions without a lattice threshold formula or a transitivity assumption. The example refutes the explicitly declared all-supercritical interpretation of Benjamini's 2013 Problem 9.6. The original question omits its probability quantifier; no unique author intent, exclusive priority, or current open status is asserted.",
      "native_version": "1.0.0",
      "publication_date": "2026-10-22",
      "DOI": "10.5281/zenodo.23573603",
