      "MAIN_SHA256": "ecc56322f381f86fec5c3e05cfd9656c8e1c96d932696ef93eab06daf34be019",
      "title": "A telescoping proof of the focal antipedal sum invariant",
      "SEO_title": "A telescoping proof of the focal antipedal sum invariant | Alec Kriebel",
      "description": "A positive-distance identity proves equality of the two focal antipedal sums for regular closed elliptic billiard orbits, including admitted odd periods and stars.",
      "rights": "CC BY 4.0; manuscript and original authored support files",
      "abstract": "Reznik, Garcia and Koiller observed that the sums of the distances from the two foci of an ellipse to their respective antipedal vertices agree along every closed elliptic billiard orbit. We prove this equality for every regular closed orbit tangent to a strictly nested confocal ellipse, including odd primitive periods, star orbits and repeated traversals. The difference of the two ordinary positive antipedal distances on each edge is a fixed coefficient times the vertical displacement of that edge. Closure therefore gives the equality without a parity restriction.",
      "native_version": "1.0",
      "publication_date": "2026-10-06",
      "DOI": "10.5281/zenodo.23191247",
      "source_schema": {
        "@context": "https://schema.org",
        "@type": "ScholarlyArticle",
        "@id": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23191247",
